From a0ddcc4e8367c0d134e14df14ea74efb190fb0fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:14:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban show: say what wakes a scheduled card on the
 status line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`hermes kanban show` printed `status: scheduled` and the wake check in a separate
field below Diagnostics, while the run line carried the raw `SCHEDULED_UNTIL=...`.
An agent that grepped `status:|→` quoted that deadline to David as the wake time
when it was only the backstop: the card had a wake check that would wake it the
moment the awaited card landed (defect agent-3a632ca054).

New sibling hermes_cli/kanban_wake_summary.py renders one wake for every
card-status surface:
- CLI `status:` line: `scheduled — wakes when `<cmd>` passes (next probe HH:MM),
  backstop YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM`, or `scheduled — wakes at <time>` with no check.
  The status word stays the first token (awk '{print $2}' parsers keep working).
- `--json` and the kanban_show tool: `wakes: {check, next_probe_at, backstop_at}`
  (null when not scheduled).
- worker_context: a `Wakes:` header line after Workspace (ctx_workspace_span's
  offset is unchanged).
The backstop is `kanban_timed_park.implied_wake` of the latest parking event.
Display only; scheduling is unchanged.

Test: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_show_wake.py (all 6 red on e2d7c95bb9).
